libmidas (1.1.2-0ddebs11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * debian/control : fixed Build-Depends syntax, added Multi-Arch: same,
    removed obsolete Pre-Depends, rewrote the descriptions
  * debian/rules : use dh_autoreconf so the regenerated files are
    cleaned, remove the .la file directly, enable all hardening flags
  * debian/patches : removed 01_update_scripts.patch, LT_INIT is already
    in the orig configure.ac
  * debian/patches/01_64bit-pointer-alignment.patch : fix the truncation of
    the buffer pointers to 32 bits, MIDASinit() crashed on 64-bit
    architectures
  * debian/patches/02_fixed-size-32bit-types.patch : U32 and S32 are now
    32-bit on 64-bit architectures, loading XM, IT and S3M modules failed
  * debian/patches/03_s3m-pattern-pointers.patch : fix a heap overflow,
    loading S3M modules crashed on 64-bit architectures
  * debian/README.Debian : added, documents the unsupported compressed
    IT 2.14 samples
  * debian/source/lintian-overrides : override ancient-libtool for the
    unused upstream ltconfig
  * debian/*.dirs, debian/not-installed.in : removed, not needed
  * debian/copyright : added Housemarque Inc., fixed Upstream-Name
  * debian/README.source : updated

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:50:27 +0100

